        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "935900ee-a83f-330d-b1b7-093156aa0d9a",
                "word": "orthographique",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "420a95e1-9152-4561-b243-1223f125c7f6",
                        "entry_id": "935900ee-a83f-330d-b1b7-093156aa0d9a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "orthographiques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "79933cbe-825c-3e29-b635-081cc58a39b5",
                        "entry_id": "935900ee-a83f-330d-b1b7-093156aa0d9a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui est relatif à l’orthographe."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "20f226b2-95f2-40e6-9e24-6f0897c871e8",
                                "sense_id": "79933cbe-825c-3e29-b635-081cc58a39b5",
                                "text": "Il est possible que le hasard de la politique amène un jour au ministère un homme assez instruit pour savoir que le préjugé orthographique ne se justifie ni par la logique, ni par l’histoire, mais seulement par une tradition relativement récente, qui s’est formée surtout d’ignorance, assez intelligent aussi pour comprendre que rien ne sera fait pour le progrès de l’enseignement primaire tant que de si courtes années d’études devront être employées principalement à enseigner aux enfants à lire et à écrire, comme en Chine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6a7a833-2b94-4c60-b9b5-2460f875e48f",
                                "sense_id": "79933cbe-825c-3e29-b635-081cc58a39b5",
                                "text": "Les sempiternels débats sur la norme orthographique sont aujourd’hui encore la cause de bien des réactions épidermiques. Il est de bon ton de faire passer les réformateurs pour de dangereux extrémistes et notamment pour des phonographistes convaincus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f7481a6-731b-4c73-b5e8-24f247b48fc2",
                                "sense_id": "79933cbe-825c-3e29-b635-081cc58a39b5",
                                "text": "Prenant acte de la diffusion d’une « écriture inclusive » qui prétend s’imposer comme norme, l’Académie française élève à l’unanimité une solennelle mise en garde. La démultiplication des marques orthographiques et syntaxiques qu’elle induit aboutit à une langue désunie, disparate dans son expression, créant une confusion qui confine à l’illisibilité."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ff451ad5-6bf5-3f5a-a343-09aa14aa06ef",
                        "entry_id": "935900ee-a83f-330d-b1b7-093156aa0d9a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Ce qui appartient à l’orthographie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2aa630f8-75db-4c5d-acd0-3c165ff037dc",
                                "sense_id": "ff451ad5-6bf5-3f5a-a343-09aa14aa06ef",
                                "text": "Un dessin orthographique. Projection orthographique de la sphère."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "aee8652e-4e5d-4e03-8888-76d49c089d3a",
                        "source_entry_id": "935900ee-a83f-330d-b1b7-093156aa0d9a",
                        "target_lang_word": "spelling",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "spelling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e2cec1e-8674-3e26-ac7f-8c76923b8b9c",
                                        "entry_id": "935637cb-f5d1-32c4-ad38-6a536603c218",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "present participle and gerund of spell"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "gerund",
                                            "participle",
                                            "present"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3be8cfc8-d2b6-4b55-a582-3e16aeffe6e6",
                                                "sense_id": "5e2cec1e-8674-3e26-ac7f-8c76923b8b9c",
                                                "text": "[p 88] A persuasive theory about the authority of the quarto or Folio texts might shed light on how Shakespeare actually spelt these names in a particular manuscript, but, since Shakespeare seemed capable of spelling his own name differently on different occasions, how reliable a guide would such evidence be?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "spelling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b4194e92-b1cf-38dd-86da-fc24e3340311",
                                        "entry_id": "dda81089-a4d8-3cce-b41b-bec33e1b5784",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act, practice, ability, or subject of forming words with letters, or of reading the letters of words; orthography."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54af681d-c772-4929-a9c4-b7496d8a0840",
                                                "sense_id": "b4194e92-b1cf-38dd-86da-fc24e3340311",
                                                "text": "For the practical use of spelling comes in writing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dba4e96b-b277-424a-a81b-ee8995737f6e",
                                                "sense_id": "b4194e92-b1cf-38dd-86da-fc24e3340311",
                                                "text": "Spelling was invented by man and, like other human inventions, is capable of development and improvement by man in the direction of simplicity, economy, and efficiency."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80f600ca-89a6-4941-8369-33ca5ceb5549",
                                                "sense_id": "b4194e92-b1cf-38dd-86da-fc24e3340311",
                                                "text": "I knew that Kriciak, the inspector who was supervising me for the Marshals Service, was going to go nuts when I told him that I wanted to allow Landon to participate in soccer and spelling."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93cfa5b3-b115-3374-9b0b-f238ae309bf1",
                                        "entry_id": "dda81089-a4d8-3cce-b41b-bec33e1b5784",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The manner of spelling of words; correct spelling."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a15b057c-751b-4800-bec5-cab4dde341f1",
                                                "sense_id": "93cfa5b3-b115-3374-9b0b-f238ae309bf1",
                                                "text": "Because Elizabethan spelling was fluid, editors feel free to ‘modernize’ (correct) the spelling in the quartos and the Folio. But how is one to spell Rosencratz or Guildenstern, where the spelling varies, not only from text to text, but even within texts?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a32c956-91b9-3987-9e54-0b3448af7e92",
                                        "entry_id": "dda81089-a4d8-3cce-b41b-bec33e1b5784",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A specific spelling of a word."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6196f590-a7d7-4a19-9a77-e17ce17f14fb",
                                                "sense_id": "2a32c956-91b9-3987-9e54-0b3448af7e92",
                                                "text": "[p 253] *excellent Q2’s ‘extent’ is generally dismissed as an error, probably a mis-reading of ‘exlent’, a common spelling at this time.\n[p 269] reverend The spellings ‘reuerent’ (Q2) and ‘Reuerend’ (F) were interchangeable at this time.\n[p 466] Guildensterne and Rosincrance are F’s consistent spellings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29d4cddc-7b81-3c79-a2ed-be8c526b97bd",
                                        "entry_id": "dda81089-a4d8-3cce-b41b-bec33e1b5784",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A spelling test or spelling bee."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "countable",
                                            "dated",
                                            "rare",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5ad971f1-a95d-4f8c-80db-f6b5c28dc12b",
                                                "sense_id": "29d4cddc-7b81-3c79-a2ed-be8c526b97bd",
                                                "text": "The boys were anxious for a spelling in the evening but I said no."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9ecad749-78c5-4093-84cd-bce92a7697b6",
                                                "sense_id": "29d4cddc-7b81-3c79-a2ed-be8c526b97bd",
                                                "text": "How her face ust to look, in the twilight, / As I tuck her to spellin’; and she / Kep’ a-hummin’ that song ’tel I ast her, / Pine-blank, ef she ever missed me!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa3396a1-9f69-4725-9fcf-8cdc4da2c3f9",
                                                "sense_id": "29d4cddc-7b81-3c79-a2ed-be8c526b97bd",
                                                "text": "So we'd sit with these girls during school hours, and we told them, if they'd slip off, that we'd get away, and we'd go to [the school] to a spelling."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "68d98b93-4f69-3f1e-8a69-b5d5a87a650c",
                                        "entry_id": "dda81089-a4d8-3cce-b41b-bec33e1b5784",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A choice of notation among enharmonic equivalents for the same pitch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d0710f9-4db3-4919-b069-51cce173654c",
                                                "sense_id": "68d98b93-4f69-3f1e-8a69-b5d5a87a650c",
                                                "text": "The spelling of a pitch is strongly influenced by its harmonic and melodic context."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7ccd7a31-bbde-47ab-afc6-61dac197940a",
